# Pictures, rich content and embedded pages

Images can explain a room or make a device easier to recognise. They must not become the only way to find its state or operate it. Treat household artwork, actual camera imagery and external websites as different content sources with different evidence and privacy needs.

<h2 id="pictures">Picture card families</h2>

| Native family | Purpose | Required alternative |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Picture | An image, optionally with an explicit navigation or action behaviour | A useful name for the destination/action; informative alternative text only when the image adds meaning. |
| Picture entity | An entity-associated image or supported camera view | Entity name, current state and image time/source when relevant. |
| Picture glance | Image context plus several entity indicators/actions | The same named states and actions in a keyboard-accessible reading order. |
| Picture elements | Positioned state labels, badges, icons, images, conditional elements and action buttons | A normal-flow list of equivalent named information and operations. |

A decorative room drawing is not a live view. A retained camera image is not current footage. Use [camera guidance](cameras.html#ha-ctrl-015-states) for image freshness and stream failures. Missing artwork must leave names, states and actions intact. Do not crop away meaningful hazard or access information.

