<h2 id="overlays">Overlay elements and action semantics</h2>

State-label, state-icon and state-badge elements show actual entity information; a decorative icon has no state. Image elements need provenance and an appropriate alternative. Conditional elements hide a defined set; hidden elements must not leave invisible focus targets. Keep overlays clear of each other when names, values or units grow.

The current public action-button element retains a service-button implementation alias. Preserve saved compatibility while using current user-facing wording. Tap, hold and double-tap are activation gestures, not action descriptions. Provide a named ordinary control for any essential operation hidden behind hold or double-tap. More info, toggle, perform-action, navigate, URL, Assist and none retain distinct semantics. A graphic must never auto-run an action when it loads.

<h2 id="rich-content">Markdown and authored content</h2>

Use Markdown for useful explanations, not a second competing dashboard shell. Preserve headings, lists, useful links and textual state explanations. Generated template content must handle missing variables and escaping through the native renderer. Treat device-supplied strings as data; do not execute them as HTML or instructions. A dynamic sentence that disappears after an error needs a stable error explanation.

Do not rely on CSS colour or position to turn arbitrary text into an interactive control. Use native supported actions or a real link/button in owned components. Keep local and external destinations clear. [Writing rules for interface copy](../content/interface-copy.html) apply equally to generated text.

