<h2 id="embeds">External webpages and blocked content</h2>

A Webpage card can embed an external origin or a local `/local` file. The theme cannot guarantee that origin's typography, accessibility, availability, content policy or sign-in behaviour. Do not weaken browser restrictions to make an iframe load. Name the provider and purpose, preserve the native security settings, and offer an ordinary link when embedding is blocked or inappropriate. Explain that opening the external page leaves Home Assistant; do not claim it is a local setting.

Do not place tokens, passwords or household identifiers in demonstration URLs. Avoid automatically loading sensitive external feeds on shared displays. A blank iframe is a loading/failure problem, not evidence that the household has no data. The specimen below uses a static unavailable state and a verified public documentation destination; it does not load a third-party frame.

