<h2 id="acceptance">Acceptance checks</h2>

Test overlays with long translations at 320px and zoom, broken images, an unavailable entity and a blocked iframe. Reach every essential action without coordinates, holding or double-tapping. Turn images off: named controls and state remain understandable. Check keyboard focus cannot enter hidden conditional elements. Confirm opening a page makes no device request and no external media is fetched before the chosen privacy boundary.

Sources: [Picture elements](https://www.home-assistant.io/dashboards/picture-elements/), [Picture entity](https://www.home-assistant.io/dashboards/picture-entity/), [Webpage](https://www.home-assistant.io/dashboards/iframe/), [Markdown](https://www.home-assistant.io/dashboards/markdown/), and [dashboard actions](https://www.home-assistant.io/dashboards/actions/).

<h2 id="evidence">Implementation and evidence boundary</h2>

This is a reference design specification, not a replacement for native Home Assistant components. The examples use invented records and local draft feedback; they do not call Home Assistant. Mapping a registry entry here establishes a design owner, not proof that every integration, browser or device has been tested. Keep native state formatting, translations, permissions, capabilities and event handling. Theme tokens can change presentation; they cannot supply missing application behaviour.

The [interface coverage inventory](../reference/ha-interface-coverage.json) records the finite source baseline and exact mappings. Recheck native behaviour after frontend changes. Use the [native task acceptance process](native-task-accessibility.html) to record what was actually tested.

Apply the [design styles](../styles/index.html), [writing guide](../content/index.html), [layout](../styles/layout.html), [colour roles](../styles/colour.html) and [typography](../styles/typography.html). Structural dividers use the quiet border token; editable boundaries and focus indicators remain distinct. Preserve 16px native control text, visible labels, keyboard access and readable names at 320px. A compact arrangement must not remove a capability explanation or essential recovery route.

Review owner: civica maintainers. Source baseline: Home Assistant Core 2026.11.1 and frontend 20261028.5; primary documentation reviewed on 12 November 2026.
